{{Short description|Football tournament group stage}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=May 2018}}
'''Group 3 of the 1978 FIFA World Cup''' was one of four groups of nations competing at the [[1978 FIFA World Cup]], consisting of [[Brazil national football team|Brazil]], [[Austria national football team|Austria]], [[Spain national football team|Spain]] and [[Sweden men's national football team|Sweden]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/78full.html |title=World Cup 1978 finals |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref>

In their first World Cup appearance since [[1958 FIFA World Cup|1958]], [[Austria national football team|Austria]] retrieved some of their [[Wunderteam|past glory]], finishing ahead of a [[Zico (footballer)|Zico]] and [[Rivellino]]-led [[Brazil national football team|Brazil]]. The ''Seleção'' clinched second place and faced South American rivals [[Argentina national football team|Argentina]] and [[Peru national football team|Peru]] in the second round.

